    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 1,
      "sourceSentenceId": 1,
      "chunkId": "s35-p01",
      "image": "assets/images/01.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p01.mp3",
      "en": "When a child first picked up a crayon, a line might have been the first mark he made.",
      "cn": "当一个孩子第一次拿起蜡笔时，画出的第一个痕迹可能就是一条线。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 2,
      "sourceSentenceId": 2,
      "chunkId": "s35-p02",
      "image": "assets/images/02.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p02.mp3",
      "en": "Then he learned to draw a straight line with the help of a ruler.",
      "cn": "然后，在尺子的帮助下，他学会了画直线。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 3,
      "sourceSentenceId": 3,
      "chunkId": "s35-p03",
      "image": "assets/images/03.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p03.mp3",
      "en": "He used lines to write numbers, symbols, and the letters of the alphabet.",
      "cn": "他用线条来写数字、符号和字母表中的字母。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 4,
      "sourceSentenceId": 4,
      "chunkId": "s35-p04",
      "image": "assets/images/04.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p04.mp3",
      "en": "The lines on a map helped him find the best route from one place to another.",
      "cn": "地图上的线条帮他找到从一个地方到另一个地方的最佳路线。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 5,
      "sourceSentenceId": 5,
      "chunkId": "s35-p05",
      "image": "assets/images/05.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p05.mp3",
      "en": "He also used lines to draw pictures.",
      "cn": "他还会用线条画画。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 6,
      "sourceSentenceId": 6,
      "chunkId": "s35-p06",
      "image": "assets/images/06.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p06.mp3",
      "en": "Lines are everywhere.",
      "cn": "线条无处不在。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 7,
      "sourceSentenceId": 7,
      "chunkId": "s35-p07",
      "image": "assets/images/07.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p07.mp3",
      "en": "You can see lines in the grain of a piece of wood or in the cracks on a narrow sidewalk.",
      "cn": "你可以在一块木头的纹理或狭窄人行道的裂缝中看到线条。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 8,
      "sourceSentenceId": 8,
      "chunkId": "s35-p08",
      "image": "assets/images/08.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p08.mp3",
      "en": "You can see lines outside a building or in the field.",
      "cn": "你也可以在建筑物外或田野里看到线条。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 9,
      "sourceSentenceId": 9,
      "chunkId": "s35-p09",
      "image": "assets/images/09.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p09.mp3",
      "en": "Lines are also used to create art.",
      "cn": "线条还可以用于艺术创作。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 10,
      "sourceSentenceId": 10,
      "chunkId": "s35-p10",
      "image": "assets/images/10.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p10.mp3",
      "en": "In drawing, line is an element of art that is the path of a moving point through space.",
      "cn": "在绘画中，线条是一种艺术元素，它是一个移动的点在空间中的轨迹。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 11,
      "sourceSentenceId": 11,
      "chunkId": "s35-p11",
      "image": "assets/images/11.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p11.mp3",
      "en": "Artists use lines to lead your eyes through a work of art.",
      "cn": "艺术家用线条来引导你的视线去浏览艺术作品。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 12,
      "sourceSentenceId": 12,
      "chunkId": "s35-p12",
      "image": "assets/images/12.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p12.mp3",
      "en": "A line can be drawn on paper with a pencil or scratched into wet clay with a stick.",
      "cn": "线条可以用铅笔在纸上画出，也可以用棍子在湿黏土上刻划。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 13,
      "sourceSentenceId": 13,
      "chunkId": "s35-p13",
      "image": "assets/images/13.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p13.mp3",
      "en": "Depending on its direction, a line can express different ideas or feelings.",
      "cn": "根据其方向，线条可以表达不同的思想或情感。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 14,
      "sourceSentenceId": 14,
      "chunkId": "s35-p14",
      "image": "assets/images/14.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p14.mp3",
      "en": "Lines are used to express different images in Chinese calligraphic drawing.",
      "cn": "在中国书法绘画中，线条被用来表现不同的意象。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 15,
      "sourceSentenceId": 15,
      "chunkId": "s35-p15",
      "image": "assets/images/15.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p15.mp3",
      "en": "The word calligraphy means beautiful handwriting.",
      "cn": "“书法”一词的意思是漂亮的笔迹。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 16,
      "sourceSentenceId": 16,
      "chunkId": "s35-p16",
      "image": "assets/images/16.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p16.mp3",
      "en": "In China, calligraphy is used to form characters that represent the language.",
      "cn": "在中国，书法用于书写代表语言的汉字。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 17,
      "sourceSentenceId": 17,
      "chunkId": "s35-p17",
      "image": "assets/images/17.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p17.mp3",
      "en": "Characters are more than just a letter of the alphabet.",
      "cn": "汉字不仅仅是字母表中的一个字母。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 18,
      "sourceSentenceId": 18,
      "chunkId": "s35-p18",
      "image": "assets/images/18.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p18.mp3",
      "en": "They can represent an idea, an object, or a verbal sound.",
      "cn": "它们可以代表一个想法、一个物体或一个语音。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 19,
      "sourceSentenceId": 19,
      "chunkId": "s35-p19",
      "image": "assets/images/19.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p19.mp3",
      "en": "Calligraphic lines are usually made with brush strokes that change from thin to thick in one stroke.",
      "cn": "书法线条通常是一笔完成，笔画从细到粗逐渐变化。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 20,
      "sourceSentenceId": 20,
      "chunkId": "s35-p20",
      "image": "assets/images/20.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p20.mp3",
      "en": "To make a thin line, artists use the tip of the brush.",
      "cn": "为了画出一条细线，艺术家们会使用毛笔的笔尖。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 21,
      "sourceSentenceId": 21,
      "chunkId": "s35-p21",
      "image": "assets/images/21.webp",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s35-p21.mp3",
      "en": "As you press on the brush and more of it touches the paper, the line becomes wider.",
      "cn": "当你按压笔刷，有更多的刷毛接触到纸时，线条就会变得更宽。"
    }
  ]
